The period for a subpulse to reappear at a same phase is defined by P_{3}=\\hat{P}_{3}/n, where n\\propto r_{\\rm D} is the number of sparks in a circle. Since both the IAG and the ICG have the same height h and hence, the same \\Delta r, from Eq.(1) one gets

